# Wave W17-R (Route 126 Trench): door wall — arched crater rock: a dark warm crater rock laid in arch courses — a band of lighter voussoir stones standing across its upper face, seamed like the Crater Door’s own arch repeated along every wall the door’s road passes (design: the great arched Crater Door in the east wall; the wall kind carries the arch register, art layer only — the shipped door dressing itself stands byte-preserved). Route 126 Trench’s own wall — darker and warmer than Route 124 Trench’s blue-grey jointed shaft rock, and the fleet’s only arch-banded wall.
